# --- ask_kind
@pq108 fact
  holds question_text ask_kind "{{prefix}}{{message}}\n>>>\n\nWhich kind of answer from the list does the request want? Reply with the number only."
@pq109 fact
  holds answer_format ask_kind number
@pq110 fact
  holds establishes ask_kind kind
@pq111 fact
  holds asserts ask_kind kind
@pq112 fact
  holds priority ask_kind 10
@pq113 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 1 yesno
@pq114 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 1 "yes or no: whether something is true, holds, is allowed or is absent (for example: Is Ana a doctor? May Ion work on 2026-04-01? Is Ana older than Ion?)"
@pq115 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 2 reach
@pq116 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 2 "whether one thing can be reached from another through a chain of links (for example: Can one get from A to B without passing a closed point?)"
@pq117 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 3 list
@pq118 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 3 "the names of the things that fit (for example: Who works at Acme? Which cities are in Spain?)"
@pq119 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 4 value
@pq120 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 4 "one stored value of something: an amount, a total, a size, a date, a difference (for example: What is the total pay of Sales? What is the age of Ana?)"
@pq121 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 5 count
@pq122 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 5 "how many different things fit (for example: How many people work at Acme?)"
@pq123 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 6 highest
@pq124 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 6 "the thing with the highest or largest value (for example: Who earns the most at Acme?)"
@pq125 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 7 lowest
@pq126 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 7 "the thing with the lowest or smallest value (for example: Which city is the smallest?)"
@pq127 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 8 puzzle
@pq128 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 8 "numbers for unknowns (x, y) that must satisfy given equations or limits (for example: Let x and y be integers from 0 to 5; is there an assignment with x + y = 4?)"
@pq129 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 9 every
@pq130 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 9 "whether all, none, most or at least some number of the members of a group fit (for example: Is everyone at Acme certified? Do most members hold a licence?)"
@pq131 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 10 when
@pq132 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 10 "when something held, since when, until when, or for how long (for example: When did Ana work at Acme? How long has Ion lived in Cluj?)"
@pq133 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 11 why
@pq134 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 11 "why something is true: its reason or explanation (for example: Why is Ana eligible?)"
@pq135 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 12 statement
@pq136 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 12 "nothing is asked: the user states a fact (for example: Ana works at Acme.)"
@pq137 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 13 only_greeting
@pq138 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 13 "the whole message is only a greeting, with nothing to look up (for example: Hello! Good morning.)"
@pq139 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 14 only_thanks
@pq140 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 14 "the whole message is only thanks, with nothing to look up (for example: Thanks! Thank you very much.)"
@pq141 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 15 only_closing
@pq142 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 15 "the whole message is only a goodbye, with nothing to look up (for example: Bye! See you.)"
@pq143 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 16 only_apology
@pq144 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 16 "the whole message is only an apology, with nothing to look up (for example: Sorry!)"
@pq145 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 17 only_feeling
@pq146 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 17 "the whole message only shows a feeling, with nothing to look up (for example: I am lost... This is great!)"
@pq147 fact
  holds choice ask_kind 18 none
@pq148 fact
  holds choice_text ask_kind 18 "nothing to look up: an order to do something, or no request (for example: ok. Write a poem. Keep the door closed.)"

